@Hammer power-up: projectile / mode hooks.
@
@ REVISION: the previous version of this file made mode 10 work by REPLACING the mode-2
@ test at each site:
@
@     cmp r1, #2   ->   cmp r1, #0xa
@
@ That is not an addition, it is a substitution. Every one of those sites is followed by a
@ conditional branch, so rewriting the constant changed the meaning from "is this Fire?"
@ to "is this Hammer?". Fire Flower stopped being able to throw. Observed symptom: with
@ the full record set, receiving a Fire Flower produced no fireballs at all; with only the
@ gate records, Fire Flower threw normally.
@
@ A single ARM `cmp` cannot express "mode == 2 or mode == 10", so these sites are NOT
@ patched here. Mode 2 keeps its original behaviour exactly, and Hammer's throwing path
@ must be provided by real code in subsdk0 via a `hook` with a trampoline -- which is now
@ possible because the DT_INIT defect that made every subsdk0 build break rendering has
@ been fixed (see docs/SUBSDK0_DT_INIT_ROOT_CAUSE.md).
@
@ Only ADDITIVE patches remain in this file. An additive patch accepts every value the
@ retail instruction accepted and adds mode 10; it can never remove a behaviour.

execute_mode_mask:
    @ Projectile execute: widen the mode bitmask from 0x64 (bits 2,5,6) to 0x464 (bits
    @ 2,5,6,10). Pure addition: 0x464 & 0x64 == 0x64, so every previously accepted mode
    @ still passes and bit 10 is now accepted too.
    type:    instr
    instruction: movw r3, #0x464
    address: 0x007AB000

@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@ REMOVED - destructive substitutions. Do not reintroduce without a real hook.
@
@   can_change_to_hammer    0x007A2708   cmp r3,#8   -> movhi r3,#1
@       `sub_607A26F8` has 0 callers in the image: dead code. Dropped as pointless.
@
@   check_set_fireball_mode 0x007AA9BC   cmp r1,#2 -> #0xa
@   set_fireball_action_mode0x007AAA88   cmp r0,#2 -> #0xa
@   create_fireball_a_mode  0x007AABB8   cmp r0,#2 -> #0xa
@   create_fireball_b_mode  0x007AAC94   cmp r0,#2 -> #0xa
@   execute_mode_guard      0x007AAFF4   cmp r1,#6 -> #0xa
@   execute_mode_guard2     0x007AB0E4   cmp r0,#2 -> #0xa
@       Each removed the retail mode from the branch condition. These are the cause of
@       "fire flower appears but nothing fires".
@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
